---
Render ONE clean canonical reference image for a Vibemon creature named "{{ vibemon.identity.name }}".

STYLE BIBLE (attached reference images)
- Match the rendering style of the attached style bible images — outline weight, shading steps, texture level, and cozy handheld scale.
- Palette muting from the style bible applies to clothing and props only — preserve accurate skin tone, hair color, and facial features from the subject reference.
- The style bible shows how to render, not which character or clothes to assign — do NOT copy reference characters' faces, skin tones, ethnicities, poses, or exact wardrobes.

{% include "_style/rendering.j2" %}

PURPOSE
- This image will be used as the visual reference for a later nine-pose sprite sheet.
- Prioritize locked anatomy, readable silhouette, exact proportions, exact palette, and exact signature feature placement over dramatic posing.
- The creature must be easy to copy into many poses without redesigning it.

CANVAS RULES
- Background: flat matte {{ vibemon.aesthetic.background_color.hex }} ({{ vibemon.aesthetic.background_color.name }}) as ONE uniform wash filling every pixel that is not the creature. This is a chroma-key screen for compositing — paint it as a fully saturated, pure {{ vibemon.aesthetic.background_color.hex }}, exactly that hex, not a muted, greyed, or desaturated approximation. This exact key color must NEVER appear anywhere on the creature (body, lineart, eyes, highlights, or accents); shift any creature color that would collide with it.
- The background must stay perfectly flat — no paper texture, grain, vignette, or dither on the background. Texture and grain apply to creature fills only.
- The background contains nothing else. No scenery, props, text, labels, UI, grid, glow, aura, floor line, weather marks, or decorative effects.
- Draw exactly one full-body creature in a neutral three-quarter view, turned just enough to show the back/dorsal silhouette and appendage roots clearly.
- Keep the whole creature inside frame with margin on all sides.

ISOLATION (creature only — no ground or flourish)
- The creature is isolated in an empty matte void. Battle ground and shadows are added later by the game — never bake them into this image.
- The lowest drawn pixels must be the creature's feet, paws, belly, tail tip, or other body part. Nothing may appear below them.
- Do NOT draw: drop shadow, contact shadow, cast shadow, oval shadow pool, ground patch, dirt smear, grass tufts, pebbles, floor line, horizon, platform, pedestal, or floating particles outside the body.
- No speed lines, sparkles, hearts, sweat drops, tear drops, question marks, exclamation points, or other expression shorthand.
- No drop shadow baked into the sprite.

IDENTITY
- Name: {{ vibemon.identity.name }}
- Element(s): {{ vibemon.elements | join(" / ") }}
{% if vibemon.identity.visual_notes %}
- Personality notes (do not infer anatomy from these): {{ vibemon.identity.visual_notes }}
{% endif %}

PRIMARY ELEMENT — {{ vibemon.elements[0] | upper }} (canonical anatomy, palette, and motifs — the source of truth for what this creature looks like). The BODY ARCHETYPE below dictates the silhouette type. Role and tier modify posture, scale, and complexity but NEVER override the body archetype.
{% include "elements/" ~ vibemon.elements[0] ~ ".j2" +%}

{% if vibemon.elements | length > 1 %}
SECONDARY ELEMENT — {{ vibemon.elements[1] | upper }} (accent layer only: extremities, markings, secondary materials — must never override the primary element's silhouette or palette)
{% include "elements/" ~ vibemon.elements[1] ~ ".j2" +%}

{% endif %}
TIER
{% include "tiers/" ~ vibemon.identity.tier ~ "/visual.j2" +%}

ROLE
{% include "roles/" ~ vibemon.identity.battle_role.name | lower ~ ".j2" +%}
Role body-language cues describe attitude only. They must never add humanoid arms, hands, legs, shoulders, fists, palms, or upright posture if the chosen body archetype does not naturally have them.

{% if vibemon.identity.provider_visual_notes %}
INFLUENCES (surface treatment ONLY — express as palette, texture, markings, or sheen on the body the archetype above defines; never change silhouette, body plan, limb count, appendages, or posture; no detached effects):
- {{ vibemon.identity.provider_visual_notes }}
{% endif %}

LOCKED DESIGN DECISIONS
- Choose one simple body plan from the primary element's BODY ARCHETYPE.
- Choose the exact appendage configuration once: number, type, root placement, size, and major shape for every arm, leg, flipper, wing, tail, fin, crest, shell, antenna, or tentacle.
- Choose at most the allowed number of signature features from the tier complexity budget.
- If a dorsal fin, shell, membrane, crest, mane, plate, tail, or other back feature exists, make its root, outline, size, and internal marking unmistakable. It must be attached anatomy, not a cape, prop, halo, or detached object.
- Do not include any alternate forms, extra pose variants, action marks, expressive symbols, or environmental storytelling.

PALETTE & STYLE
- Primary fill: {{ vibemon.aesthetic.primary_color }} — overrides the PRIMARY ELEMENT's color hex if they differ.
{% if vibemon.elements | length > 1 %}
- Secondary fill (accent zones — extremities, markings, underbelly): {{ vibemon.aesthetic.secondary_color }}
{% endif %}
- Lineart: #3D2B1F Tobacco Brown. Never pure black or darker than #2A1E16.
- Highlights: #F5F5DC Cream. Never pure white.
- Highlights must stay inside the creature silhouette only.
- Body shading only: warm-shifted darker variants of each fill zone, mixed toward Tobacco Brown. Shading stays ON the creature body — never as a separate shadow shape on the matte.

{% include "_style/rendering.j2" %}

FINAL CHECK BEFORE DRAWING
- The image must look like the definitive model of one creature, not a scene and not a pose sheet.
- Every non-matte pixel belongs to the creature body or outline. Zero ground marks, grass tufts, or shadow pools on the matte.
- Every future pose should be able to copy this exact silhouette, proportions, palette, appendage count, and signature feature placement.
